1. **An ultrasonic welding-control device**, comprising:  

   an elongate probe body defining a longitudinal probe axis and having a coupling portion configured to be acoustically coupled to at least one workpiece undergoing ultrasonic welding, the coupling portion including a convex outer surface elongated in a first direction extending along the longitudinal probe axis;  

   an ultrasonic transducer array supported by the probe body beneath the convex outer surface, the ultrasonic transducer array comprising a plurality of individually addressable transducer elements distributed along a concave array surface elongated in a second direction extending along the longitudinal probe axis, the concave array surface facing the convex outer surface such that ultrasonic energy transmitted by the transducer elements propagates through the coupling portion and exits the probe body through the convex outer surface;  

   wherein the first direction and the second direction, when projected onto a common plane containing the longitudinal probe axis, define a nonzero acute angle β relative to one another, such that the concave array surface is obliquely oriented relative to the convex outer surface while each of the convex outer surface and the concave array surface extends longitudinally along the probe body;  

   drive circuitry coupled to the ultrasonic transducer array and configured to apply independently controlled excitation signals to respective transducer elements to transmit a steered or focused ultrasonic beam through the convex outer surface toward a weld region of the at least one workpiece;  

   receive circuitry coupled to the ultrasonic transducer array and configured to acquire echo signals produced by ultrasonic energy reflected from the weld region; and  

   a controller operatively coupled to the drive circuitry, the receive circuitry, and an ultrasonic welding apparatus, the controller being configured to:  

   determine, from the echo signals, at least one weld-condition parameter indicative of formation or quality of a weld in the weld region;  

   compensate beam steering, focusing, or echo processing for the angle β and for curvature of at least one of the convex outer surface or the concave array surface; and  

   generate, based on the at least one weld-condition parameter, a control output that causes the ultrasonic welding apparatus to adjust or terminate at least one welding parameter selected from welding amplitude, welding frequency, welding force, welding energy, and welding duration.
